    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 1614: Maximum Nesting Depth of the Parentheses (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given a valid parentheses string s, return the nesting depth of s. The nesting depth is the
                maximum number of nested parentheses at any point in the string.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "(1+(2*3)+((8)/4))+1"<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: The digit 8 is inside three nested parentheses in the string, which is the
                deepest level reached.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int maxDepth(string s) {
        int maxDepth = 0, currentDepth = 0;

        for (char ch : s) {
            currentDepth += (ch == '(') - (ch == ')');
            maxDepth = max(maxDepth, currentDepth);
        }

        return maxDepth;
    }
};</code></pre>
